                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Summary:[/h1]\nA Sirius Game is a game where you take control of Sirius, a bad guy from family of traders, who decides to leave home and... sail until he die, trading and escorting ships meanwhile. Is that all? No, you can shoot your cannons to protect others, you can even cast magic! But now the important question - is it fun to play the role of Sirius, doing mostly a boring messenger work combined with repetitive cannon shooting to protect NPC ships? Not at all. Only thing worth mentioning and praising is the way story is being presented, with dialogues in style you may know from visual novels.\n\n[h1]Pros:[/h1]\n- [b]Story parts[/b]. I guess this is the reason why Aldorlea Games took this game under their publishing, the character and background artworks are nice, same applies to dialogues.\n- Mediocre 3D graphics.\n\n[h1]Cons:[/h1]\n- [b]Boring[/b]. Ships are slow and the sea combat is just average relatively for the genre.\n- Controls with keyboard are awful, but mouse control is just a little better.\n- Everytime I tried to get to the options menu the game crashed, so I had to play it only in small window.",
